From 449fe416f449243a41425d07849cf7d60d22e999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:34:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Microsoft Azure as a second Cloud VPS provider (VM
 management)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Azure joins UpCloud as an active provider in the Cloud VPS section, scoped
to virtual machines (create/list/detail/start/stop/restart/delete), same
as the user asked ("почти всё, но только с виртуальными серверами").

- bot/services/azure_api.py: new ARM REST client using Service Principal
  (client-credentials OAuth2) auth. Handles ARM's async semantics — every
  create/delete/power action polls the resource's own
  provisioningState/instanceView until it reaches a terminal state, since
  the initial PUT/POST response only reflects the desired state. VM
  creation orchestrates the full resource chain a VM needs (resource
  group -> VNet/subnet -> public IP -> NSG -> NIC -> VM), reusing one
  resource group and one VNet per (account, location) so repeat creates
  don't pile up duplicate infrastructure, and delete cleans up the VM's
  own NIC/public IP/NSG afterwards. Curated (not full-Marketplace) image
  and VM-size catalogs keep the picker usable instead of listing Azure's
  200+ raw sizes.

- cloud_store.py: generalized to store arbitrary provider-specific
  credential fields (tenant_id/client_id/client_secret/subscription_id
  for Azure) instead of hardcoding username/password, since Azure's auth
  shape has no equivalent to UpCloud's login.

- Account connect is a 4-step wizard (Tenant ID, Client ID, Client
  Secret, Subscription ID) instead of UpCloud's username+password, since
  Azure has no plain API login — the Client Secret message is deleted
  right after receipt like a password. VM creation reuses the same
  password-vs-SSH-key choice already built for UpCloud/Node.

Verified against a fake Azure ARM server exercising the full flow
end-to-end: wrong-credential rejection, the 4-field connect wizard, VM
creation via both auth paths (including the multi-resource orchestration
and its progress callback), list/detail/start/stop/restart/delete, and
the async polling logic actually looping (not just checking once) for
provisioning state, power state, and deletion.

